//! Tauri application layer for Network Monitor.
//!
//! Owns the process: the single tokio runtime, window/tray lifecycle, persistence and
//! the IPC surface. Business logic lives below in `nm-core`/`nm-probes`; this crate
//! wires it to the UI as typed commands (UI -> Rust) and typed events (Rust -> UI),
//! whose TypeScript definitions are generated by `tauri-specta` — never hand-written.
//!
//! # The shape of a running app
//!
//! [`run`] starts three long-lived tasks and then gets out of the way:
//!
//! * `runtime` probes the baselines and the monitored applications' discovered endpoints,
//!   and pushes a health snapshot once a second — but only while the window is visible.
//!   Hidden means "stop drawing", never "stop measuring".
//! * `settings` writes the configuration back to disk, debounced, so a dragged slider is
//!   one write rather than one per frame.
//! * `heartbeat` proves the event channel is alive before the first measurement lands.
//!
//! Tests live in `tests/` rather than in `#[cfg(test)]` modules; see `tests.manifest`
//! for the Windows loader constraint that forces this, and note that the library target
//! sets `test = false`, so an in-crate test module would never run at all.

